[ceiling] Required flat lower boundary of the female connector seat and its lead slot. The cap prints crown-down, with the supported-face allowance on this machine-floor face. Supports have a 4.6 mm-deep open seat and leave through its aft mouth or the crown slot before the connector is installed. Ear plates, screws and inserts retain their separate mounting datums; this answer does not transfer the coupon's fit result to the full cap.
alternatives: A ramp intruding into the seat changes the connector's required stadium clearance; ramping outward removes additional cap stock beside the lead route. An open slot through the floor removes the enclosure boundary beneath the connector. The flat seat keeps the specified body envelope and uses its accessible mouth/crown support path.
