[ceiling] Required routing floors of the two crown grooves, 4 mm wide and 3.5 mm into the cap's bed face. Each groove opens directly to the crown and joins an open motor-terminal well, so supports are removed through the bed-side opening before wiring. The groove defines routing space; assembled lead restraint and printed roof finish are separate qualifications.
alternatives: A V-section with the same depth reduces the space for the two insulated leads; retaining that space requires a deeper or wider cut through the cap. Cutting through the cap removes the floor and its connection between the seat and terminal wells. The open flat-bottom grooves preserve the specified wire envelope and support access.
